  "question": {
    "text": "There is a uniform electrostatic field in a region. The potential at various points on a small sphere centred at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, in the region, is found to vary between the limits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>589</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>589</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. What is the potential at a point on the sphere whose radius vector makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the direction of the field?"
  },
